@@ -133,4 +135,10 @@
 Models reflections on rough surfaces by distributing outgoing rays around the perfect mirror reflection direction, controlled by a shininess exponent $\alpha$ [S1, unofficial]. It computes the dot product between the reflection vector $\vec{R}$ and view direction $\vec{\omega}_r$, clamps it to $[0, \infty)$, and raises it to the power of $\alpha$ to determine the intensity of the glossy highlight [S1, unofficial].
 
+### Ray Reflection Tracing
+Traces reflected rays to simulate mirror-like reflections, limited to a maximum recursion depth [S4, unofficial]. It initializes a traversal variable, marches along the reflected ray, checks for intersections, and shades the hit point using the scene normal and material properties [S4, unofficial]. If no hit occurs, it returns the background color [S4, unofficial]. The provided implementation limits reflections to 1 bounce [S4, unofficial].
+
+### Water Reflection
+Water reflects the sky it is under rather than a static authored color, making low sun angles optimal for lake visuals [S5, unofficial]. Swimming underwater limits sight distance to 34 meters and removes red light from the scene [S5, unofficial].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of light sources and objects in the scene for each ray, due to intersection tests and shadow ray casts [S2, unofficial].
